<div class="pb-[40px]">
    <div class="pb-[20px]">
        <h3 class="text-display-24 md:text-display-32 font-semibold">Policy Insights for Decision Makers</h3>
        <p class="font-light text-display-14 md:text-display-16">The findings of SOFI 2026 highlight that achieving Zero Hunger in Southeast Asia requires a shift from production-oriented policies toward integrated agrifood systems transformation. For ASEAN Member States, three strategic priorities emerge.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-[20px] md:gap-[30px]">
        <div class="border-[D3D3D3] border-[1px] rounded-2xl flex flex-col gap-[10px]">
            <span class="text-display-24 md:text-display-32 text-[#B39354] font-semibold">01</span>
            <h6 class="text-display-18 md:text-display-24 font-semibold">Make Healthy Diets the Primary Goal of Agrifood Systems</h6>
            <p class="font-light text-display-14 md:text-display-16">Food security policies should move beyond ensuring adequate calorie availability to improving the affordability and accessibility of healthy diets. Governments should invest in diversified agricultural production, nutrition-sensitive value chains, and food environments that enable consumers to make healthier dietary choices. Integrating nutrition objectives into agricultural planning will simultaneously improve public health, reduce malnutrition in all its forms, and strengthen rural livelihoods (FAO et al. 2026).</p>
        </div>

        <div class="border-[D3D3D3] border-[1px] rounded-2xl flex flex-col gap-[10px]">
            <span class="text-display-24 md:text-display-32 text-[#B39354] font-semibold">02</span>
            <h6 class="text-display-18 md:text-display-24 font-semibold">Build Resilient and Climate-Smart Food Systems</h6>
            <p class="font-light text-display-14 md:text-display-16">Climate resilience should become a central pillar of agricultural development. Scaling climate-smart agriculture, sustainable natural resource management, digital agriculture, and early warning systems will help farmers adapt to climate risks while maintaining productivity and reducing environmental impacts. Regional cooperation on food reserves, climate information, agricultural statistics, and food safety standards will further strengthen ASEAN's resilience to future shocks (ASEAN 2025; ADB 2023).</p>
        </div>

        <div class="border-[D3D3D3] border-[1px] rounded-2xl flex flex-col gap-[10px]">
            <span class="text-display-24 md:text-display-32 text-[#B39354] font-semibold">03</span>
            <h6 class="text-display-18 md:text-display-24 font-semibold">Strengthen Science, Innovation, and Regional Collaboration</h6>
            <p class="font-light text-display-14 md:text-display-16">Achieving agrifood systems transformation requires stronger investments in agricultural research, innovation, digital technologies, and human capital. Institutions such as SEARCA can play a pivotal role by generating evidence, strengthening the science–policy–practice interface, developing future agricultural leaders, and facilitating regional knowledge sharing. Through these efforts, SEARCA can support ASEAN Member States in translating regional commitments into tangible improvements in food security, nutrition, resilience, and sustainable rural development.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>